# AES-256-GCM master key used by internal/snmpx to derive per-record
# encryption keys via HKDF-SHA256. The same value MUST be loaded by
# the snmp, alert, and api services or the at-rest credential / webhook
# secret store becomes unreadable.
#
# Copy this file before editing:
#   cp secrets/snmp_master.example secrets/snmp_master
# Then replace the placeholder with 32+ random bytes:
#   openssl rand -base64 32 > secrets/snmp_master
#
# The real ./secrets/snmp_master file is gitignored. Never commit a
# real key. In production the value is sourced from Azure Key Vault
# via Workload Identity (see deploy/helm/flowscope/values.yaml).
#
# Replace the next line (and delete these comments) with your key:
dev-only-master-key-CHANGE-ME-32-bytes-min
